  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: Daily bank reconciliation\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** Bank movements are matched against the ledger every working day. The hourly cost is deliberately unknown to show that unknown cost is never treated as zero.\n- **Owner:** Treasury\n- **Executions per month:** 22\n- **Steps:** 4\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 26.77\n- **Monthly cost:** unknown\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 2 | Match transactions to ledger | HYBRID | RECOMMENDED | AI | 16.50 | 60 |\n| 3 | Investigate unmatched items | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 7.33 | 0 |\n| 4 | Sign off reconciliation | RULE_BASED | REQUIRED | RULES | 1.83 | 55 |\n\n- **Match transactions to ledger:** Input is digital structured and integration readiness is partial.\n- **Investigate unmatched items:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is unknown.\n- **Sign off reconciliation:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 12.47\n- **Gross monthly savings:** unknown\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** unknown\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** not applicable\n- **ROI at 12 months:** not applicable\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / DATA] Export bank statement handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / DATA] Match transactions to ledger handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Investigate unmatched items depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Sign off reconciliation is business critical\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Export bank statement:** REQUIRED. handles sensitive data; Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Match transactions to ledger:** RECOMMENDED. handles sensitive data\n- **Investigate unmatched items:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Sign off reconciliation:** REQUIRED. requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Export bank statement: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Match transactions to ledger: HYBRID, with a person reviewing a sample or the flagged cases\n4. Investigate unmatched items: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n5. Sign off reconciliation: RULE_BASED, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n6. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
